  "notes": "The related noun ⟦{呪|のろ}い→呪い：15822_noroi⟧ means 'curse.' This word appears frequently in horror, folklore, and fantasy contexts, but is also used figuratively to express deep resentment (e.g., cursing one's fate or bad luck).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{呪|のろ}い→呪い：15822_noroi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦かける→かける：00854_kakeru⟧ — to cast a curse\n- ⟦{呪|のろ}い→呪い：15822_noroi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{解|と}く→解く：02301_toku⟧ — to break a curse\n- ⟦{運命|うんめい}→運命：06879_unmei⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{呪|のろ}う — to curse one's fate\n- {呪|のろ}われた⟦{場所|ばしょ}→場所：00829_basho⟧ — cursed place\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{呪|のろ}い→呪い：15822_noroi⟧ — curse (noun)\n- ⟦{呪文|じゅもん}→呪文：11843_jumon⟧ — spell, incantation\n- ⟦{祟|たた}り→祟り：22000_tatari⟧ — divine curse, retribution",
